/-!
# Candidate affine matrix space for the reconstruction argument

The 124 packed matrices below specify a linear space of 50 by 50 matrices.
The predicate `AffineRestriction g` means that the displacement action of `g`
is the identity plus a member of this explicit space. This is independent
finite data: neither membership of a source-hypothesis matrix in the affine
space nor the chart reconstruction theorem is assumed or asserted here.

Numerical discovery: the right-stabilizer algebra of the mixed radical forms,
intersected with its adjoint for the displacement pairing, has three scalar
composition factors. The displayed space is the candidate kernel of those
three scalar maps. These descriptions remain certificate obligations.
See `KernelEquations/source/README.md` for matrix provenance and conventions.
-/

